menu "espix SSH"

    config ESPIX_SSH_ENABLED
        bool "Enable the SSH server"
        default y
        help
            A minimal SSH server written on PSA Crypto.

            Note that this is a hand-written implementation of a security
            protocol, not a reviewed one. It is appropriate for a trusted LAN
            and inappropriate for exposure to the internet.

    config ESPIX_SSH_PORT
        int "Listen port"
        depends on ESPIX_SSH_ENABLED
        range 1 65535
        default 22

    config ESPIX_SSH_MAX_SESSIONS
        int "Concurrent connections"
        depends on ESPIX_SSH_ENABLED
        range 1 4
        default 2
        help
            How many SSH connections may be open at once.

            Two is the useful minimum: scp and sftp open their own connection,
            so with a limit of one no file could be transferred while an
            interactive session was open. Each connection costs about 22KB —
            roughly 14KB of packet buffers and stored key-exchange state, plus
            the connection task's stack — so raising this is not free on a part
            with a few hundred KB of internal RAM.

    config ESPIX_SSH_TASK_STACK
        int "Connection task stack (bytes)"
        depends on ESPIX_SSH_ENABLED
        range 4096 16384
        default 8192
        help
            The protocol logic is shallow, but the shell session runs on this
            stack, and commands run on it too.

    config ESPIX_SSH_TASK_PRIO
        int "SSH task priority"
        depends on ESPIX_SSH_ENABLED
        range 1 10
        default 4
        help
            Above loaded apps so a busy app cannot starve a login, below the
            console so the serial line stays usable as a recovery path.

endmenu
